# `$` not starting `$left`/`$right`, a lone `&`, and `@` not followed by a quote.
mode: syntax
---- query
from t | where $foo & x;
@x
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..28
  PIPELINE@0..23
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "t"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    WHERE_OP@9..14
      IDENT@9..14 "where"
    WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
    ERROR@15..23
      ERROR@15..16 "$"
      IDENT@16..19 "foo"
      WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
      ERROR@20..21 "&"
      WHITESPACE@21..22 " "
      IDENT@22..23 "x"
  SEMICOLON@23..24 ";"
  WHITESPACE@24..25 "\n"
  ERROR@25..27
    ERROR@25..26 "@"
    IDENT@26..27 "x"
  WHITESPACE@27..28 "\n"

error[DS0001]: unexpected character `$`
  --> query:1:16
  |
1 | from t | where $foo & x;
  |                ^ not valid here
  |
  = help: `$` is only used in `$left` and `$right`

error[DS0001]: unexpected character `&`
  --> query:1:21
  |
1 | from t | where $foo & x;
  |                     ^ not valid here
  |
  = help: to combine conditions, use `and`

error[DS0001]: unexpected character `@`
  --> query:2:1
  |
2 | @x
  | ^ not valid here
  |
  = help: a verbatim string is `@` followed directly by a quote: `@'C:\data'`
